{"id":"nombre","es":"nombre","en":["name"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"m. Your first name. Your surname is el apellido.","sent":{"es":"¿Cuál es tu {nombre}?","en":"What is your name?"}}
{"id":"apellido","es":"apellido","en":["surname"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"m. Colombians carry two: the father's, then the mother's.","sent":{"es":"¿Cómo se escribe su {apellido}?","en":"How do you spell your surname?"}}
{"id":"vida","es":"vida","en":["life"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"f. mi vida is also a term of endearment.","sent":{"es":"Así es la {vida}.","en":"That is life."}}
{"id":"padres","es":"padres","en":["parents"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"m. pl. Means parents, not fathers, unless the context says otherwise.","sent":{"es":"Mis {padres} viven en Inglaterra.","en":"My parents live in England."}}
{"id":"abuela","es":"abuela","en":["grandmother","grandma"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"f. abuelo for grandfather, abuelos for grandparents.","sent":{"es":"Mi {abuela} cocina muy rico.","en":"My grandmother cooks really well."}}
{"id":"primo","es":"primo","en":["cousin"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"m. prima for a female cousin.","sent":{"es":"Mi {primo} vive en Cali.","en":"My cousin lives in Cali."}}
{"id":"tio","es":"tío","en":["uncle"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"m. In Spain also mate, but not in Colombia.","sent":{"es":"Mi {tío} tiene una finca.","en":"My uncle has a farm."}}
{"id":"tia","es":"tía","en":["aunt"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"f.","sent":{"es":"Voy a visitar a mi {tía}.","en":"I am going to visit my aunt."}}
{"id":"sobrino","es":"sobrino","en":["nephew"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"m. sobrina for a niece.","sent":{"es":"Mi {sobrino} tiene cinco años.","en":"My nephew is five."}}
{"id":"nieto","es":"nieto","en":["grandson","grandchild"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"m. nieta for a granddaughter, nietos for grandchildren.","sent":{"es":"Mi abuelo tiene diez {nietos}.","en":"My grandfather has ten grandchildren."}}
{"id":"pareja","es":"pareja","en":["partner","couple"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"f. even for a man: mi pareja es Juan.","sent":{"es":"Vine con mi {pareja}.","en":"I came with my partner."}}
{"id":"chica","es":"chica","en":["girl","young woman"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"f. Casual, for a woman of about your own age. niña is a child.","sent":{"es":"Esa {chica} es mi compañera de clase.","en":"That girl is my classmate."}}
{"id":"parce","es":"parce","en":["mate"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"Medellín slang, short for parcero. Friendly and very informal.","sent":{"es":"¿Qué más, {parce}?","en":"How is it going, mate?"}}
{"id":"cliente","es":"cliente","en":["customer","client"],"pos":"noun","topic":"work","note":"Same form for a man or a woman.","sent":{"es":"El {cliente} siempre tiene la razón.","en":"The customer is always right."}}
{"id":"companero","es":"compañero","en":["colleague","classmate"],"pos":"noun","topic":"work","note":"m. compañera for a woman. compañero de cuarto is a flatmate.","sent":{"es":"Mi {compañero} de trabajo es de Bogotá.","en":"My colleague is from Bogotá."}}
{"id":"policia","es":"policía","en":["police officer","police"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"la policía is the police force. el policía or la policía for one officer.","sent":{"es":"Llame a la {policía}.","en":"Call the police."}}
{"id":"mesero","es":"mesero","en":["waiter"],"pos":"noun","topic":"food","note":"m. The Colombian word. mesera for a waitress. Spain says camarero.","sent":{"es":"El {mesero} nos trajo la carta.","en":"The waiter brought us the menu."}}
{"id":"conductor","es":"conductor","en":["driver"],"pos":"noun","topic":"travel","note":"m. conductora for a woman.","sent":{"es":"El {conductor} del bus fue muy amable.","en":"The bus driver was very kind."}}
{"id":"enfermera","es":"enfermera","en":["nurse"],"pos":"noun","topic":"body","note":"f. enfermero for a man.","sent":{"es":"La {enfermera} me tomó la temperatura.","en":"The nurse took my temperature."}}
{"id":"ingeniero","es":"ingeniero","en":["engineer"],"pos":"noun","topic":"work","note":"m. ingeniera for a woman. Colombians address engineers as ingeniero, like a title.","sent":{"es":"Soy {ingeniero}.","en":"I am an engineer."}}
{"id":"invitado","es":"invitado","en":["guest"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"m. invitada for a woman.","sent":{"es":"Eres mi {invitado}.","en":"You are my guest."}}
{"id":"dueno","es":"dueño","en":["owner"],"pos":"noun","topic":"people","note":"m. dueña for a woman.","sent":{"es":"El {dueño} del apartamento vive arriba.","en":"The owner of the flat lives upstairs."}}
{"id":"cuerpo","es":"cuerpo","en":["body"],"pos":"noun","topic":"body","note":"m.","sent":{"es":"Me duele todo el {cuerpo}.","en":"My whole body aches."}}
{"id":"brazo","es":"brazo","en":["arm"],"pos":"noun","topic":"body","note":"m.","sent":{"es":"Me rompí el {brazo}.","en":"I broke my arm."}}
{"id":"pierna","es":"pierna","en":["leg"],"pos":"noun","topic":"body","note":"f.","sent":{"es":"Me duele la {pierna}.","en":"My leg hurts."}}
{"id":"espalda","es":"espalda","en":["back"],"pos":"noun","topic":"body","note":"f. The body part. Coming back is volver.","sent":{"es":"Tengo dolor de {espalda}.","en":"I have backache."}}
{"id":"diente","es":"diente","en":["tooth"],"pos":"noun","topic":"body","note":"m. Plural dientes. lavarse los dientes, to brush your teeth.","sent":{"es":"Me duele un {diente}.","en":"I have a toothache."}}
