{"id":"pastilla","es":"pastilla","en":["pill","tablet"],"pos":"noun","topic":"body","note":"f.","sent":{"es":"Tómate una {pastilla} cada ocho horas.","en":"Take one tablet every eight hours."}}
{"id":"drogueria","es":"droguería","en":["chemist's","pharmacy"],"pos":"noun","topic":"body","note":"f. The everyday Colombian word. farmacia is understood too.","sent":{"es":"¿Hay una {droguería} cerca?","en":"Is there a chemist's nearby?"}}
{"id":"cita","es":"cita","en":["appointment","date"],"pos":"noun","topic":"body","note":"f. Both the doctor and the romantic kind.","sent":{"es":"Tengo {cita} con el médico mañana.","en":"I have a doctor's appointment tomorrow."}}
{"id":"accidente","es":"accidente","en":["accident"],"pos":"noun","topic":"body","note":"m.","sent":{"es":"Hubo un {accidente} en la autopista.","en":"There was an accident on the motorway."}}
{"id":"emergencia","es":"emergencia","en":["emergency"],"pos":"noun","topic":"body","note":"f. In Colombia, dial 123.","sent":{"es":"Es una {emergencia}.","en":"It is an emergency."}}
{"id":"ayuda","es":"ayuda","en":["help"],"pos":"noun","topic":"body","note":"f. Shouted for help, ¡auxilio! is more urgent.","sent":{"es":"Necesito {ayuda}.","en":"I need help."}}
{"id":"embarazada","es":"embarazada","en":["pregnant"],"pos":"adjective","topic":"body","note":"A famous trap: it does not mean embarrassed. That is avergonzado, or qué pena.","sent":{"es":"Mi hermana está {embarazada}.","en":"My sister is pregnant."}}
{"id":"sed","es":"sed","en":["thirst"],"pos":"noun","topic":"food","note":"f. tener sed, to be thirsty.","sent":{"es":"Tengo mucha {sed}.","en":"I am very thirsty."}}
